# Install at /opt/validator3/validator3.env  (root:root 0600 — SECRETS FILE).
# Loaded via `env_file:` in docker-compose.validator3.yml. The binary maps env
# names onto its viper flags (DATA_DIR -> --data-dir, POS_VALIDATOR_SEED ->
# --pos-validator-seed, ...).
#
# ⚠️⚠️⚠️ POS_VALIDATOR_SEED IS THE ONLY SECRET IN THIS FILE ⚠️⚠️⚠️
# It is VALIDATOR 3'S BLS MNEMONIC.
#   • NEVER commit it to any repository — the repo contains PUBLIC KEYS ONLY.
#   • On launch day, POS_VALIDATOR_SEED must contain the SAME mnemonic that the
#     bootstrap script consumed from VALIDATOR3_BLS_SEED when it registered
#     validator 3 on-chain (backend/scripts/pos/validator_bootstrap/). The node
#     votes in the validator mesh with this BLS key; a mismatched key means the
#     node will not be able to sign votes/blocks for its registered identity.
#   • Operator writes this line at deploy time; leave it EMPTY in the repo copy.
POS_VALIDATOR_SEED=

# Chain data inside the container (bind-mounted: /opt/validator3/data/chain).
DATA_DIR=/data
# glog logs inside the container (bind-mounted: /opt/validator3/data/logs).
LOG_DIR=/logs

# --- public reference values for validator 3 (NOT secrets) --------------------
# DeSo identity (transactor) key the bootstrap script derives from VALIDATOR3_SEED:
#   FS13vXnYzpczMkW9Hbk3czZLs4nwSwwu23hhsbHQoZ2oiFJwkGF1rh
# Registered on-chain domain (covered by the existing node.forked.social DNS
# record — the port keeps the P2P listeners distinct):
#   node.forked.social:42300
